<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim Nasir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1926">1926</a>–<a href="/years/2008">2008</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim Nasir was prime minister of the Maldives under the sultanate from 1957. His government suppressed the secessionist United Suvadive Republic in the southern atolls in 1959–1963 and negotiated independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1965. After the monarchy was abolished he became the first president of the republic in 1968, developing tourism, until 1978.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibrahim-nasir.jpg" alt="Ibrahim Nasir" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The President's Office of the Republic of Maldives · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ibrahim_Nasir.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
